  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_038 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, concat) is the clear best at 0.7207 acc / 0.6815 F1, and all its individual components (scvi_n200 over pca_n2000, multiprofile over singleprofile, transformer over avgpool, imagenet_vit_l over resnet50, multimodal over unimodal) are supported by prior experiments. However, the fusion strategy has only been tested as 'concat' in this top-performing regime. Question: config_039 changes only the fusion from concat to weighted, directly testing whether learned modality weighting can further improve over a fixed concatenation in the best-known setting. Rationale: This is the highest-value exploitation step—every other hyperparameter is already at its empirically best value, so isolating the fusion choice gives a clean read on whether this design axis still has headroom. If weighted fusion helps, it identifies a new improvement direction; if it does not, it confirms concat is sufficient and redirects budget toward other untested axes (e.g., alternative image encoders or profile counts). Under a limited budget, this single-variable change from the current best is the most informative next experiment."
}

